encounter_log.csv
# Real employee data / notes dropped into the project folder (PII / PHI)
*EMR_notes*
Active Associates*.xlsx
# HC renames its export between runs — the 8-25-26 one arrived as "Navarre Active
# Employees 8.25.26.xlsx" and matched none of the rules above. These are full employee
# rosters (PII): match on what they ARE, not on one report title.
*Active Employees*.xlsx
*Navarre*.xlsx
*Associates*.xlsx
EMR Easy Enter Worksheets.xlsx
# Backups of roster.xlsx (real roster PII), like roster.xlsx itself. Broad on
# purpose: any roster.<something>.xlsx is a dated/labelled copy of the real roster.
# (roster_template.xlsx uses an underscore, so it is NOT caught by this.)
roster.*.xlsx
# Retired: the builder now reads Department/Division from the roster directly, so it
# no longer generates this. Kept ignored so any leftover copy can't be committed.
work_titles.csv
# Which work titles / shifts the builder hides. Local UI state.
builder_prefs.json
# Stray / scratch files
Untitled-*.txt
# Office lock files (e.g. ~$Active Associates....xlsx) — created while a workbook is
# open. Their names can echo a PHI filename, so keep them out of the tree entirely.
~$*

